WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.003 --> 00:00:04.755
Hello, I'm Ed Sheeran

00:00:04.838 --> 00:00:06.507
and I'm an English
singer-songwriter

00:00:06.590 --> 00:00:08.842
auditioning to be
in the British Money Heist.

00:00:08.926 --> 00:00:11.637
Yes, welcome. Tell us a
little bit about yourself.

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:13.472
So, I'm a singer and...

00:00:13.555 --> 00:00:15.516
I've been a liar,
I've been a thief.

00:00:15.599 --> 00:00:16.642
Sorry, what was that?

00:00:16.725 --> 00:00:17.559
Don't worry.

00:00:17.643 --> 00:00:19.937
I was just
thinking out loud.

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:21.813
I'm here to audition
for Glasgow

00:00:21.897 --> 00:00:22.856
'cause I hear he's,
you know,

00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:24.358
the British version
of Berlin.

00:00:24.441 --> 00:00:26.151
And I thought
it would be a good fit.

00:00:26.235 --> 00:00:27.861
Right, perfect.

00:00:27.945 --> 00:00:28.862
Well, first off,

00:00:28.946 --> 00:00:30.572
and I don't want to step
on your toes here,

00:00:30.656 --> 00:00:32.783
but I thought we could
change the character's name

00:00:32.866 --> 00:00:34.910
from Glasgow to Ipswich.

00:00:34.993 --> 00:00:36.745
Just 'cause it's a little
bit more personal to me,

00:00:36.828 --> 00:00:38.080
you know, and
if I'm gonna do the role...

00:00:38.163 --> 00:00:40.666
Alright, Ed Sheeran
as Ipswich.

00:00:41.291 --> 00:00:42.167
Take one.

00:00:43.335 --> 00:00:44.920
Do you know what five
divorces mean?

00:00:45.587 --> 00:00:47.047
It's five times
I've been in love.

00:00:47.631 --> 00:00:49.591
Let the matriarchy begin.

00:00:49.675 --> 00:00:51.093
Yeah, I know
that's Nairobi,

00:00:51.176 --> 00:00:52.344
I just wanted to say that.

00:00:52.427 --> 00:00:55.639
Este es un momento
maravilloso.

00:00:55.722 --> 00:00:56.557
Okay, another one.

00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:59.142
This is a wonderful moment.

00:00:59.226 --> 00:01:01.812
This is a wonderful moment.

00:01:01.895 --> 00:01:04.147
This is a wonderful moment.

00:01:04.565 --> 00:01:06.567
So I know Pedro Alonso
is an amazing singer

00:01:06.650 --> 00:01:08.193
and I love that scene
at the wedding

00:01:08.277 --> 00:01:09.278
but for the UK version,

00:01:09.361 --> 00:01:10.821
I thought
I could sing this one...

00:01:11.613 --> 00:01:14.199
Baby, I'm

00:01:14.783 --> 00:01:17.369
dancing in the dark

00:01:18.036 --> 00:01:20.455
with you between my arms.

00:01:21.290 --> 00:01:23.709
Barefoot on the grass,

00:01:24.543 --> 00:01:26.753
listening to our
favourite song...

00:01:27.546 --> 00:01:29.923
-What do you think?
-What else can you show us?

00:01:30.007 --> 00:01:33.886
My bad habits lead to big
heists stealing some gold.

00:01:33.969 --> 00:01:37.306
Conversations with my
brother singing Bella Ciao.

00:01:37.389 --> 00:01:40.809
Swearing this will be the
last, but it probably won't.

00:01:40.893 --> 00:01:43.937
I got nothin' left to lose,
or use, or do.

00:01:44.438 --> 00:01:46.440
I know I've lived my life
like a son of a bitch

00:01:46.523 --> 00:01:48.901
but I feel like dying
with dignity.

00:01:52.863 --> 00:01:55.073
I'd also love to audition
for the Professor.

00:01:58.202 --> 00:01:59.161
Welcome.

00:01:59.244 --> 00:02:01.538
We are gonna rob
Buckingham Palace.

00:02:02.164 --> 00:02:03.248
Let me tell you how.

00:02:03.332 --> 00:02:04.833
Do you know
what Aikido means?

00:02:04.917 --> 00:02:06.502
Do you know
what Aikido means?

00:02:08.337 --> 00:02:09.338
Inspector?

00:02:10.214 --> 00:02:11.173
What are you wearing?

00:02:11.924 --> 00:02:12.883
Inspector.

00:02:13.425 --> 00:02:14.718
What are you wearing?

00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:17.221
So, what do you think?

00:02:17.304 --> 00:02:18.805
Well, yeah,
I loved it but...

00:02:19.473 --> 00:02:21.642
Really, there's someone
else who has the last word

00:02:21.725 --> 00:02:23.685
on all the auditions
for the show.

00:02:24.269 --> 00:02:25.979
-Hello Ed.
-Hey.

00:02:26.063 --> 00:02:26.980
What are you wearing?

00:02:28.273 --> 00:02:29.107
Just kidding.

00:02:29.733 --> 00:02:31.944
Hey, I liked your take
on the Professor.

00:02:32.027 --> 00:02:35.656
You almost got
the glasses trick right.

00:02:37.241 --> 00:02:38.659
Personally I think
I see you more

00:02:38.742 --> 00:02:40.786
as one of the members
of la banda.

00:02:41.328 --> 00:02:44.081
-Ipswich, right?
-Yes.

00:02:44.164 --> 00:02:49.169
Hey, listen I really like
your Buckingham Palace idea.

00:02:50.254 --> 00:02:51.755
So, I have business
proposal.

00:02:52.923 --> 00:02:57.094
How does 2.4 billion Pounds
sound to you?

00:02:57.886 --> 00:02:58.720
Tell me more.

00:03:03.642 --> 00:03:05.352
So, I've got a suggestion

00:03:05.435 --> 00:03:07.771
for the UK version
for a name change.

00:03:07.855 --> 00:03:09.731
If you're up for it.

00:03:17.114 --> 00:03:18.073
"Quid Game."

